{"20":[{"k":"p","t":"Self-Test"},{"k":"p","t":"RAM/ROM Test"},{"k":"p","t":"The RAM/ROM Test, as shown in Figures 3-1 and 3-2, provides a visual check of the game RAM, ROM, and associated circuitry. Ifthe RAM and ROM Test passes, the display will advance to the Switch Test."},{"k":"p","t":"The RAM/ROM Test is divided into two sections. The condition of the RAM circuitry is displayed in the bottom half of the screen. If the RAM Test passes, after about an eightsecond delay, the self-test skips to the ROM Test, and the condition of the ROM circuitry is displayed in the top half of the screen"},{"k":"p","t":"Ifa Working RAM Error message appears in the bottom"},{"k":"h","t":"half of the screen, check the RAMs at locations 6E, 7E, 6K,"},{"k":"p","t":"or 7K on the Game PCB. If the error message resembles Figure 3-1, refer to Table 3-1 for the faulty RAM locations on the Game PCB."},{"k":"p","t":"Perform the following procedure to use Table 3-1"},{"k":"p","t":"PLATT IELD RAN error ot: SO00CO rote: FS00MRead: F000"},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 3-1 RAM Test Fails"},{"k":"p","t":"Mein ROM error"},{"k":"p","t":"5 \u2018 : BOM SE 38888 scree UE eee"},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 3-2 ROM Test Fails Gauntlet"},{"k":"p","t":"Table 3-1 Faulty RAM Locations"},{"k":"h","t":"RAM Error"},{"k":"p","t":"Alpha/"},{"k":"tr","t":"Play-   Motion   ~\u2014Work-"},{"k":"h","t":"field Object ing Color*"},{"k":"tr","t":"900000   902000   904000   910000"},{"k":"p","t":"Error to to to to"},{"k":"tr","t":"Position   901FFF   903FFF   905FFF   9107FF"},{"k":"tr","t":"2XXX   6D   6c   OE   10L"},{"k":"tr","t":"X?XX   7D   7   JE   10M"},{"k":"tr","t":"XX?X   a   OF   6K   oL"},{"k":"tr","t":"XXX?   a   TF   7K   OM"},{"k":"p","t":"*10L = Intensity 10M = Red OL= Green"},{"k":"h","t":"OM = Blue"},{"k":"p","t":"Notes"},{"k":"li","t":"1. If the error message itself bas bad lettering, then the fault is most likely the alphahvorking RAMs at locations 6E, 7E, OK, or 7K. A completely blank screen or several wrong-color dots can indicate @ fault in the color RAMs at locations 10L, 10M, 9L, or 9M."},{"k":"p","t":". Note the XXXX RAM error at: DOXXXX message. if the error address is between 900000 and 901FFE, go to the 900000 to 901 FFF column in Table 3-1. Likewise, if the error address is between 902000 and 903FFE, go to the 902000 to 903FFF column."},{"k":"li","t":"2. Note the Wrote: XXXX Read: XXXX message. Find the characters that do not match between the Wrote and Read words. For example, if the displayed error address is 900000 and the data is Wrote: COO0 Read: 8000, then the error is in the first characters of the wrote/read messages (C and 8, respectively). This corresponds to ?XXX in the Error Position column of Table 3-1. Thus, the faulty RAM would most likely be at location 6D."},{"k":"p","t":"Another example is if the error address is 902060 and the data is Wrote: E015 Read: E026. Then the error is in the third and fourth characters of the wrote/read messages (15 and 26, respectively) which corresponds to XX?X and XXX? in the Error Position column of Table 3-1. Thus, the faulty RAM is most likely in locations OF and 7F. If the game shows RAM errors, press the Warrior Magic button to advance to the ROM Test."},{"k":"p","t":"If the ROM Test fails, error messages may appear in the top half of the screen as shown in Figure 3-2. If the upper (U) or lower (L) main memory ROM circuits on the Game PCB fail, a Main ROM error U or L message will appear at the top of the screen. Refer to Table 3-2 for the faulty upper or lower main memory ROM locations."},{"k":"p","t":"To exit from the RAM/ROM Test and obtain the Switch Test screen, press and hold down the Warrior Magic button for about a second, then release."}],"24":[{"k":"p","t":"Self-Test Gauntlet"},{"k":"p","t":"Table 3-5 Motion Object Test Description"},{"k":"tr","t":"Controls   Press Fire   Press Magic   Move Joystick"},{"k":"tr","t":"Warrior   Object flips horizontally.   Selects next screen.   All objects scroll together."},{"k":"tr","t":"Valkyrie   Object number increments.   Object number decrements.   Up\u2014Vertical size increases."},{"k":"p","t":"Down\u2014Vertical size decreases. Right\u2014Horizontal size increases. Left\u2014-Horizontal size decreases."},{"k":"tr","t":"Wizard   Color Palette number increments.   Color palette number decrements.   Position of object moves (horizon-"},{"k":"p","t":"tally and vertically)."},{"k":"tr","t":"EIf   Picture number increments by 1   Picture number decrements by 1.   Up\u2014Picture number increments by"},{"k":"p","t":"size. Down\u2014Picture number decrements by size."},{"k":"p","t":"Ata WARRIOR <MAGIC> button for next tes:"},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 3-8 Playfield Test"},{"k":"p","t":"to right): 2x2, 3x3, 4x 4,5x5, 6x6, 7x7, and 8x8 squares. The Motion Object Test indicates the condition of the motion-object buffer circuit. The following information is provided at the bottom of the screen:"},{"k":"li","t":"* OBJECT indicates the number of the motion object selected."},{"k":"li","t":"* PICTURE indicates the stamp number in ROM."},{"k":"p","t":"HORIZONTAL indicates the horizontal position of the object."},{"k":"li","t":"* VERTICAL indicates the vertical position of the object."},{"k":"li","t":"* SIZE indicates the number of stamps across by the number of stamps down."},{"k":"p","t":"\u00a9 COLOR PALETTE indicates the palette number for colors."},{"k":"p","t":"Perform the test procedure as described in Table 3-5."},{"k":"p","t":"3-6 Motion Gbiect Test"},{"k":"p","t":"t pied tore 88b2"},{"k":"p","t":"Cokes 1 1 prene BABirB SEH button eor*next tent."},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 3-9 Motion Object Test"},{"k":"note","t":"NOTE Upon entering the Motion Object Test, ifa single object is moved down it will partially disappear under a black horizontal bar that runs across the screen on the line above the message OBJECT:001"},{"k":"p","t":"Press the Warrior Magic button to obtain the next screen."},{"k":"h","t":"Alpha Test"},{"k":"p","t":"The Alpha Test should appear as shown in Figure 3-10. The Alpha Test indicates the condition of the alphanumerics circuit. Press the Warrior Magic button to obtain the next screen."},{"k":"p","t":"Color Test The Color Test appears as shown in Figure 3-11. The Color Test indicates the condition of the display color circuits."}],"47":[{"k":"p","t":"Gauntlet Illustrated Parts Lists"},{"k":"p","t":"Linear Power Supply Assembly Parts List"},{"k":"tr","t":"Designator   Description   Part No."},{"k":"tr","t":"cl   27,000 wE, 15 VDC Electrolytic Capacitor   29-053"},{"k":"tr","t":"cl   2-Inch-Diameter Capacitor Mounting Bracket   78-70501SC"},{"k":"tr","t":"CRI   Type-MDA3501 Bridge Rectifier   3A-MDA3501"},{"k":"tr","t":"FI   Label with Fuse Value   037639-02"},{"k":"tr","t":"Fl   4 A, 250 V, 3AG Slow-Blow Glass Cartridge-T ype Fuse (Acceptable substitute is   46-201 4002"},{"k":"p","t":"part no. 46-2014001)"},{"k":"tr","t":"FI   Panel-Mounting Non-Indicating 3AG Cartridge-Type Fuse Post   79-4411001"},{"k":"tr","t":"F2-F6.   5-Position 3AG Fuse Block with %-Inch Quick-Disconnect Terminals   79-3206"},{"k":"tr","t":"F2-F6,   Fuse Block Cover   034544-02"},{"k":"tr","t":"F2-F6   Label with Fuse Values   037641-02"},{"k":"tr","t":"F2, F4-FO   4 A, 250 V, 3AG Slow-Blow Glass Cartridge-T ype Fuse (Acceptable substitute is   46-201 4002"},{"k":"p","t":"part no. 46-2014001)"},{"k":"tr","t":"F3   25 A, 32 V, 3AG Slow-Blow Glass Cartridge-Type Fuse   46-301253"},{"k":"tr","t":"FL   RFI Filter Assembly (designation not marked)   A034630-01"},{"k":"tr","t":"J2   Power Harness Assembly   A035890-01"},{"k":"tr","t":"JB   European Voltage Plug Assembly   A037479-02"},{"k":"tr","t":"J4A   AC Harness Assembly   A034629-01"},{"k":"tr","t":"TL   Transformer Assembly (Acceptable substitute is part no. A035888-02)   A035888-01"},{"k":"p","t":"Violet Jumper Assembly A035889-01 Orange Jumper Assembly A035889-02 White Jumper Assembly A035889-04 VioletWhite Jumper Assembly A035889-05"},{"k":"p","t":"Orange/Black 